Before opening aipv20, it is necessary to configure
other contents in menuconfig.

1. Kernel type  --->
	(11) Maximum zone order
	[*] Contiguous Memory Allocator

The maximum management range supported by the
partner algorithm cannot be opened for CMA without
setting it.
After selecting 'Contiguous Memory Allocator',
you can use A to allocate continuous memory.


2. Device Drivers  --->
	Generic Driver Options  --->
		[*] DMA Contiguous Memory Allocator
		(64)Size in Mega Bytes
		(4)Maximum PAGE_SIZE order of ...

After opening 'DMA Contiguous Memory Allocator',
configure the size and page allocation method of
CMA, and recommended sizes are provided here.
The area size of 'Size in Mega Bytes' cannot exceed
the size of MEM and must be an integer multiple of
'Maximum PAGE_SIZE', such as 8, 16, 32, 64.


3. Device Drivers  --->
	Graphics support  --->
		Graphics support  --->
			[ ] jz aip driver
			[*] jz aip ver2 driver

The old AIP and AIPV2 will crash, so it is necessary
to close the old AIP before using AIP_v2.
